{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775344022-5AYVIkvqo1mh8HV1W7wc","role":"assistant","created":1775344028,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me take a different approach. Looking at the raw table data more carefully, I need to understand the table structure. The tables show the maturity schedule of securities outstanding at a given time, organized by the final maturity year of each security.\n\nLooking at the 1972 file (Outstanding February 29, 1972):\n- The table shows securities that will mature in various years\n- The left section shows securities with earlier maturity years \n- The right section shows securities with later maturity years\n\nLet me manually read through the data and identify the totals for each year from each file.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_8b5d4c779a5d472194cd0973","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me manually parse the table by looking at the HTML-like structure\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1972_03_page_45.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\n# The table structure seems to have year labels in the first column\n# Let me find all occurrences of <td>YEAR</td> followed by Total\n# Looking for pattern: <td>1972</td>...<td>Total</td>\n\n# Let me search for year markers in rows\n# Pattern to find year rows with totals\nlines = content.split('<tr>')\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    # Look for year labels\n    year_match = re.search(r'<td>(\\d{4})</td>', line)\n    total_match = re.search(r'<td>Total</td><td></td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>', line)\n    if year_match and total_match:\n        print(f\"Year: {year_match.group(1)}, Total: {total_match.group(1)}\")\n    # Also check for \"Total\" with different structure\n    if 'Total' in line and 'Total' not in line[:50]:\n        # Check what's around it\n        if re.search(r'<td>(\\d{4})</td>', line):\n            print(f\"Line {i}: {line[:300]}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
