{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775344072-2dDuRKJxAMTwu25q5TdD","role":"assistant","created":1775344091,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"This is getting confusing because of the table structure. Let me look at the actual content more carefully. The year appears in the right section of the table (for the final maturity year), and the numbers in the left side.\n\nLet me re-read the tables more carefully from the original text output. Let me extract the relevant totals manually by looking at the raw content.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_c2238bc586bd451893ec6081","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me look at the 1972 data in the original text format more carefully\n# The table shows securities by their final maturity year\n\n# From the raw text output I captured earlier:\n# For 1972 file (Outstanding Feb 29, 1972):\n# Looking at the table structure, I see:\n# - First column shows \"Final maturity\" year\n# - For 1972 maturity schedule as of Feb 1972, the table shows the TOTAL amount\n#   of securities that will mature in each calendar year\n\n# Looking at the raw output from earlier:\n# The table shows totals for each year. Let me trace through manually:\n\n# From the 1972 file text output:\n# The left side shows maturity amounts and right side shows other data\n# Looking at the row with \"Total\" in the first column section:\n# <tr><td>Total</td><td>24,221</td><td>5,027</td><td>19,194</td>\n\n# This suggests 24,221 is the total for 1972 maturity year\n\n# Let me extract using a simpler approach - look at the text format\n# The table header says \"Amount of maturities\" with columns Total, U.S. Govt accounts, All other investors\n\n# Looking at the first few data rows from 1972 file:\n# <tr><td rowspan=\"12\">1976</td>...\n# This is the row for final maturity 1976, but it shows securities maturing in 1972 on the left\n\n# Wait - I think I understand now. The table is organized by:\n# Final maturity year (column 1) | Description | Amount of maturities\n# And the right side shows another set for \"Year and month of final maturity\"\n\n# The key insight: we need to find the \"Total\" for each calendar year's maturities\n# Looking at the raw text output from my earlier read:\n# I see lines like:\n# <tr><td>Total</td><td>24,221</td><td>5,027</td><td>19,194</td>\n# This appears after listing securities that mature in 1972\n\n# Let me extract by finding rows that start with <tr><td>Total\n# and getting the first number\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1972_03_page_45.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n\n# Looking for patterns: <tr><td>Total</td><td>number</td>\n# This gives us the Total for securities in that section\npattern = r'<tr><td>Total</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>'\nmatches = re.findall(pattern, content)\nprint(\"1972 file - Found totals:\")\nfor m in matches:\n    print(f\"  Total: {m[0]}, Govt: {m[1]}, Other: {m[2]}\")\n\n# Now I need to associate these with the correct year\n# The structure is: first column shows the final maturity year\n# and then after listing securities, there's a Total row\n\n# Let me find the year labels that precede these Total rows\n# Look for pattern: <td>YEAR</td> followed by stuff then Total\nlines = content.split('<tr>')\nprint(\"\\n\\nFinding year labels before Total rows:\")\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if '<td>Total</td>' in line:\n        # Look at previous lines for year\n        if i > 0:\n            prev_line = lines[i-1]\n            year_match = re.search(r'<td[^>]*>(\\d{4})</td>', prev_line)\n            if year_match:\n                print(f\"  Year: {year_match.group(1)}\")\n            else:\n                # Check for month labels like Feb, Apr etc\n                month_match = re.search(r'<td>([A-Za-z]+)', prev_line)\n                if month_match:\n                    print(f\"  Month: {month_match.group(1)}\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
