{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775344091-ifI7gppXsp50rqTzlcIK","role":"assistant","created":1775344113,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm getting closer but I need to properly associate each Total with its year. Let me look at the raw text output again more carefully. Looking at the earlier captured output, I can see:\n\nFrom the 1972 file:\n- Looking at the table, there's securities grouped by their \"final maturity\" year\n- The first column shows \"Final maturity\" year\n- Looking at the structure:\n  - First, securities with final maturity 1976 are listed, and their total is shown as 14,731 (but this is for the RIGHT side of the table showing 1976)\n  - Then we see securities for 1972 (the left side shows securities maturing in 1972)\n\nActually wait - looking at the output again:\n- Row starts with `<tr><td rowspan=\"12\">1976</td>` - this means the row spans 12 rows and shows securities with final maturity 1976\n- But these securities include ones maturing in 1972 (the first column shows \"4/1/72-EA\", \"4/21/72\" etc - these are 1972 maturities)\n- The \"Total\" for that section is 14,731 (shown in the right side of the table for 1976)\n\nSo the structure is confusing. Let me look more carefully at the columns:\n\nLooking at the table header:\n`<tr><th rowspan=\"2\">Final maturity</th><th rowspan=\"2\">Description</th><th colspan=\"3\">Amount of maturities</th><th rowspan=\"2\">Year and month of final maturity</th>...`\n\nSo the first part is \"Final maturity\" (the year when the security will finally mature)\nAnd \"Amount of maturities\" shows the total amount\n\nBut then the right side shows \"Year and month of final maturity\" with another set of securities\n\nThis is complex. Let me just read the raw data manually from the output I have:\n\nFrom the 1972 file (page 45), looking at the table:\n- The left side shows securities by their final maturity year\n- The Total for each year appears after listing the securities for that year\n\nLooking at the output from the file more carefully:\n- When it says \"1976\" in the first column, it lists securities and their amounts\n\n\n- Then when it says \"Total\" the numbers are 14,731 for 1976\n\nI see now that the \"Final maturity\" column actually represents the YEAR when securities will mature, and the amounts listed are for the current year 1972. This is clearer from the 1973 file where the first column shows 1977 and then 1978, 1979, etc.\n\nThe pattern becomes evident when I look at the row with `<tr><td>1976</td>` followed by security descriptions like \"1-1/2% Note - 4/1/72-EA\" with their corresponding amounts. The table is organizing securities by their final maturity year, showing what's scheduled to mature in each future year.\n\nFor the 1972 file specifically, I need to locate the row where 1972 appears in the first column—that's where the total for that year would be. Looking at the totals I've identified (24,221; 22,764; 32,429; 24,785), I should cross-reference these with which year each corresponds to in the Final maturity column.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_3ce19e1167f94893ad25cb7a","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# Let me try a different approach - look at the structure by examining \n# rows that have a year in the first column followed by security descriptions\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1972_03_page_45.txt', 'r') as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nimport re\n\n# Find rows that have a 4-digit year at the start\n# The pattern should be: <tr><td>YEAR</td> or <tr><td rowspan=\"X\">YEAR</td>\n# Then look for Total in subsequent rows\n\n# Split into rows\nrows = content.split('</tr>')\n\n# Find indices of rows with year labels\nyear_rows = []\nfor i, row in enumerate(rows):\n    match = re.search(r'<td[^>]*>(\\d{4})</td>', row)\n    if match:\n        year = match.group(1)\n        year_rows.append((i, year, row[:200]))\n\n# Now find Total